LINE: '# Introduction' -> H1=True
NEW_TITLE: 'Introduction'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# The U.S. Census Bureau' -> H1=True
MERGED_HEADING: 'The U.S. Census Bureau' added to content of 'Introduction'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# The Role of the U.S. Census Bureau' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=0, title='Introduction', content_len=25
NEW_TITLE: 'The Role of the U.S. Census Bureau'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Special Census program is conducted by the U.S. Census Bureau, which is the federal government's largest statistical agency.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'As the leading source of quality data about the nation's people and economy, the Census Bureau honors privacy, protects confidentiality, shares our expertise globally, and conducts our work openly. The Census Bureau is guided on this mission by our strong and capable workforce, our readiness to innovate, and our abiding commitment to our customers.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The primary function of the Census Bureau is to conduct, every 10 years, the national census, also known as the decennial census. The primary reason for conducting the decennial census is to determine the number of seats in the U.S. House of Representatives each state will have, based on its population. But there are many other reasons why the decennial census and other censuses, including Special Censuses, are important.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Responses determines future political representation in Congress.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Population totals and breakdowns by sex, age, race, and other factors inform decisions about how more than \$675 billion is distributed annually in federal funds, grants, and support to states, counties, and communities.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Governments and businesses use census data to plan new investments, services, and jobs.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Developers use census data to build new homes and revitalize old neighborhoods.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Local governments use census data for public safety and emergency preparedness.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Residents use census data to support community initiatives involving legislation, quality-of-life, and consumer advocacy.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   The census has always been a record of our history. The 2020 Census will shape a roadmap for our future.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Special Census Overview' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=1, title='The Role of the U.S. Census Bureau', content_len=1704
NEW_TITLE: 'Special Census Overview'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# What is the Special Census Program?' -> H1=True
MERGED_HEADING: 'What is the Special Census Program?' added to content of 'Special Census Overview'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Special Census program allows governmental units to request, and pay, the Census Bureau to conduct a Special Census in their area when they deem it beneficial.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'A Special Census is a basic enumeration of population, housing units, group quarters and transitory locations conducted by the U.S. Census Bureau in the years between decennial censuses. Local residents are hired and trained to conduct the Special Census.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'During a Special Census, Field Representatives (FRs) visit assigned areas and canvass, that is, travel systematically all streets, roads, and paths in the assigned area, to find all living quarters. While canvassing, they verify or update the Census Bureau's address lists based on what they observe on the ground and through interviews with respondents. At each address identified as a housing unit for interview, FRs interview an occupant and complete a Special Census questionnaire for the household.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'To measure the quality of the work performed, the Special Census program includes several quality control (QC) checks. Field Supervisors (FSs) review FR work progress. A separate team of FSs and FRs performs QC checks on completed assignments, which includes dependent quality checks and reinterviews.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Your job as an FR is to update the Census Bureau's address lists to ensure that they are as current, complete, and accurate as possible**.** You will also interview an occupant and complete a Special Census questionnaire at each housing unit address in your assigned area.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Why is the Special Census Program Conducted?' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=2, title='Special Census Overview', content_len=1542
NEW_TITLE: 'Why is the Special Census Program Conducted?'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The purpose of the Special Census program is to give governmental units an opportunity to conduct a census for their community in the years between decennial censuses.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Receiving up-to-date census information about their communities helps local and tribal governments to:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Become eligible to receive increased state funds and grants for schools, hospitals, roads, public works, and other vital programs.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Improve the ability to plan for schools and better transportation.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Improve public safety and emergency preparedness.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Where is the Special Census Program Conducted?' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=3, title='Why is the Special Census Program Conducted?', content_len=534
NEW_TITLE: 'Where is the Special Census Program Conducted?'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'A Special Census may be taken wherever the local government determines it is beneficial: in counties, neighborhoods, governmental units, or other geographic areas in the United States and Puerto Rico.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# What is the Special Census Day?' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=4, title='Where is the Special Census Program Conducted?', content_len=200
NEW_TITLE: 'What is the Special Census Day?'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Census Bureau and the governmental unit will determine a reference date for collecting the data. This date is called the *Special Census Day*.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**It is critical that all data collected are based on the status of the address on the Special Census Day.**' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Who is Involved with the Special Census Program?' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=5, title='What is the Special Census Day?', content_len=256
NEW_TITLE: 'Who is Involved with the Special Census Program?'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Conducting a Special Census is an involved process that involves many resources to execute.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**U.S. Census Bureau Headquarters.** Developed the Special Census program, including training materials and procedures used by Regional Office (RO), Special Census Office (SCO), and field staff. Census Bureau Headquarters oversees the ROs.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Regional Office (RO).** ROs are permanent offices that coordinate and carry out survey and census field data collection programs for the Census Bureau and its customers. ROs oversee SCOs.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Special Census Office (SCO).** SCOs are temporary offices established to conduct Special Census programs. The Special Census Supervisor (SCS) in the SCO directly supervises the Field Managers (FMs).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Special Census Field Manager (FM)/QC FM.** FMs/QC FMs directly manage Field Supervisors (FSs)/QC FSs. Each FM oversees approximately six to eight FSs. Each QC FM oversees approximately four QC FSs. FMs/QC FMs train FSs/QC FSs and monitor work performance and work progress for each FS/QC FS team. FMs/QC FMs also certify FS/QC FS payroll records and advise and assist FSs/QC FSs on personnel and performance issues.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Special Census Field Supervisor (FS)/QC FS:** FSs/QC FSs directly supervise Field Representatives (FRs)/QC FRs. Each FS/QC FS oversees a team of approximately 6-8 FRs/QC FRs. FSs/QC FSs train their team, provide assignments, and monitor their team member's progress and performance as they conduct their work. FSs/QC FSs also review and certify payroll records, provide feedback on job performance, and answer work-related questions.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Special Census Field Representative (FR)/QC FR:** FRs/QC FRs are responsible for working the Special Census assignments. This work includes traveling to the assigned area, verifying, or updating the provided address list, and conducting interviews with respondents to collect data as required for the Special Census.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Overview of Your Job' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=6, title='Who is Involved with the Special Census Program?', content_len=1901
NEW_TITLE: 'Overview of Your Job'
