LINE: '# Employee Responsibilities' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=17, title='End of the Day', content_len=66
NEW_TITLE: 'Employee Responsibilities'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Title 13' -> H1=True
MERGED_HEADING: 'Title 13' added to content of 'Employee Responsibilities'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Protection under Title 13 of the U.S. Code guarantees confidentiality of census information and establishes penalties for disclosing this information. This means that only people sworn to protect Title 13 data may see information the Census Bureau collects. Protected information cannot be shared with anyone who is not sworn to maintain the confidentiality of Title 13 protected data -- including the FBI, IRS, or a court of law.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Unauthorized disclosure of confidential information by a sworn Census Bureau employee is punishable by a fine of up to \$250,000, imprisonment of up to 5 years, or both. You must never reveal census information to anyone who is not a sworn Census Bureau employee.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Data Stewardship' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=18, title='Employee Responsibilities', content_len=708
NEW_TITLE: 'Data Stewardship'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Census Bureau workforce is bound to protect confidential information by an ironclad commitment backed by Federal law. Data Stewardship means providing quality data for public good while protecting individual privacy and confidentiality. This is the Census Bureau's core responsibility. We may not release personally identifiable information.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Data Stewardship assures the Census Bureau can effectively collect high quality data to be used by its customers while meeting the legal and reporting obligations of Title 13, the Privacy Act, and other applicable statutes. Keeping the public's trust is critical to our ability to carry out our mission as the leading source of quality data about the nation's people and economy.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Ways to Maintain Confidentiality as a Data Steward' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=19, title='Data Stewardship', content_len=726
NEW_TITLE: 'Ways to Maintain Confidentiality as a Data Steward'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Here are ways you can maintain the confidentiality of all census information:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   When not working, store your Special Census materials out of view, whether at home, in a public place, or in your vehicle. Always lock your vehicle whenever Special Census materials are in it.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Do not show the address lists, maps, or completed questionnaires to anyone.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Make sure no one accompanies you when you perform Census work unless they are a sworn Census employee.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Be sure no one else can hear you if discussing Title 13 protected data with a team member or your manager in public places.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Do not share personally identifiable information (PII) with another sworn Census Bureau employee who does not have a need to know.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Always ask your manager if you are not sure whether something is considered PII.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# The Privacy Act of 1974' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=20, title='Ways to Maintain Confidentiality as a Data Steward', content_len=815
NEW_TITLE: 'The Privacy Act of 1974'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Privacy Act of 1974 requires that each Federal agency advise people of their rights when collecting information from them. Specifically, a person must know under what law the information is being collected, how the information will be used and whether they must answer.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Form SC-CN(E/S), Confidentiality Notice, contains the information required by the Privacy Act of 1974. Special Census staff must give a Confidentiality Notice to each person from whom they request census-related information. Never leave this notice at an address where no one is home or that is vacant. It must always be handed to a person.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Data Falsification' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=21, title='The Privacy Act of 1974', content_len=619
NEW_TITLE: 'Data Falsification'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Even though you and your team want to do a good job and keep on schedule, problems may be encountered. However, no matter what the circumstances, you and your team members **must not submit falsified work**. Your team members are expected to help maintain the quality of census data by following written procedures, asking questions as worded on the questionnaire, and accurately recording responses that are communicated to them.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Anyone willfully falsifying information collected under Title 13, United States Code, Section 213, can be found guilty of perjury (fabrication) and may be fined up to \$250,000 and/or imprisoned up to five years. If it is determined that the falsification was intentional, they will be removed from federal service.**' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Media Contacts While You Are Working' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=22, title='Data Falsification', content_len=751
NEW_TITLE: 'Media Contacts While You Are Working'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'As you go about your work, reporters from local newspapers or TV stations may approach you seeking an interview. They may even want to accompany you while you work. If this happens:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Stop work immediately.** Explain to the reporter(s) the Census Bureau's policy on confidentiality. Tell them they can get information by calling the Special Census Office (SCO) and provide the telephone number of your SCO. Walk away from the location where you are working and continue work in that area only after the reporter(s) have left.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Do not:**' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Allow the reporter(s) to see any of your work materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Let the reporter(s) overhear or observe any interviews you are conducting.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Divulge any information that could lead the reporter(s) to identify a person, such as a name or phone number. Title 13 guarantees respondents that all information the Census Bureau collects will be kept confidential.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Call your supervisor.** If you cannot reach your supervisor, call the SCO.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Restrictions on the Political Activities of Federal Employees' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=23, title='Media Contacts While You Are Working', content_len=981
NEW_TITLE: 'Restrictions on the Political Activities of Federal Employees'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'While you are working for the Census Bureau, you are covered by the Hatch Act, which restricts certain political activities of Federal employees. Refer to Chapter 2, Section 2.F, Political Activity, of the 11-55(RO), Administrative Handbook for Employees, , for information on activities allowed and prohibited by the Hatch Act.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Lost, Missing, or Stolen Materials' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=24, title='Restrictions on the Political Activities of Federal Employees', content_len=328
NEW_TITLE: 'Lost, Missing, or Stolen Materials'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'As a census employee, you are responsible for protecting all materials assigned to you, including your Census Bureau-issued ID badge. You must take care to protect Address Registers and questionnaires from being lost or stolen. You must also take care to protect forms and other materials containing Title 13 data that are in your possession. **You must always be able to account for these materials.**' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You are responsible for:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Using census-owned property for the sole purpose of conducting official government-related work.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Properly caring for, handling, and protecting the Address Registers, questionnaires, your Census Bureau-issued ID badge, and other materials containing Title 13 data in your possession.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Properly reporting materials that are lost, missing, or stolen [within one hour]{.underline} of the discovery.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Immediately returning all census-owned materials to your manager before transfer, reassignment, or separation from the Census Bureau.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Employees may be held financially liable for materials lost, missing, stolen, or damaged due to negligence. The criminal code of the United States also provides penalties for theft, embezzlement, conversion of, or willful damage to government property. Title 18, U.S. Code 641, provides penalties of up to \$250,000 and/or 10 years of imprisonment. The Census Bureau is committed to using any lawful and reasonable means necessary to recover property owned by the Federal government and ensuring the security of all Title 13 data in an employee's possession.**' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Lost, Missing, or Stolen Materials Containing Title 13 Data' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=25, title='Lost, Missing, or Stolen Materials', content_len=1540
NEW_TITLE: 'Lost, Missing, or Stolen Materials Containing Title 13 Data'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If you or a team member experience lost, missing, or stolen materials, including your Census Bureau-issued ID badge, the person responsible for the materials must do all the following:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If the materials are found/recovered, you must notify the Census Service Center at 1-877-343-2010, Option #1, to update them on the status.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If materials or an ID badge were [stolen]{.underline}, call the police and obtain a police report number.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Call the Census Service Center (CSC) at 1-877-343-2010 and select Option #1 for Cyber Security, Physical Security, and PII Breach Incident Reporting, to report the incident.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   This must be done within one (1) hour of the discovery of lost, missing, or stolen materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Provide the police report number (if the materials were stolen).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Obtain a case number from the Census Service Center operator.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Call your manager, inform them of the incident, and provide the case number and police report number (if the materials were stolen).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'As an FS, if a member of your team experiences lost, missing, or stolen materials, you will notify your manager of the incident and provide the case number and police report number (if the materials were stolen).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Your manager will:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Make any other required notifications to census management.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Obtain replacement materials for you from the SCO.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Obtaining Replacement Materials' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=26, title='Lost, Missing, or Stolen Materials Containing Title 13 Data', content_len=1392
NEW_TITLE: 'Obtaining Replacement Materials'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If a team member is requesting a replacement Census Bureau ID badge, they [cannot]{.underline} work until they receive the new badge.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When notifying your manager that you, or a team member, has experienced lost, missing, or stolen materials, be prepared to state which materials, for which Assignment Areas (AAs), need replacing. The SCO will replace the materials as quickly as possible.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If a payroll record or INFO-COMM is lost, missing, or stolen, the originator should recreate the form, using the copy provided to them earlier, for their records. The recreated form should be distributed following normal procedures.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Providing Replacement Assignment Packages to a Team Member' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=27, title='Obtaining Replacement Materials', content_len=623
NEW_TITLE: 'Providing Replacement Assignment Packages to a Team Member'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Work previously completed for an AA whose Address Register or questionnaires are lost, missing, or stolen, will have to be re-done.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'To avoid interviewing respondents a second time, the SCO will mark, on the Form SC-920, Address List Page, all address for which they have received a completed questionnaire. These addresses are not to be worked. Labeled Forms SC-Q, Special Census Questionnaire, will not be provided for these addresses.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The SCO will also enter on the Form SC-921, Add Page, information for any added housing units for which a completed questionnaire was received. Information for any added group quarters (GQs) and transitory locations (TLs) that was reported to the SCO on an INFO-COMM will also be entered on the Form SC-921, Add Page. Any addresses entered on the Add Page when the recreated Address Register is received are not to be worked.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When providing the replacement Address Register to the team member, review the contents, making sure they understand which addresses, and possibly areas in the AA, are not to be worked.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Training Your Team' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=28, title='Providing Replacement Assignment Packages to a Team Member', content_len=1051
NEW_TITLE: 'Training Your Team'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Introduction' -> H1=True
MERGED_HEADING: 'Introduction' added to content of 'Training Your Team'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'One of the most important tasks of your job is to conduct Field Representative (FR) training for your team. When your team is grounded in Special Census procedures and understands the importance of their work, you will be able to focus on completing your work rather than handling performance and personnel issues.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Approximately 8 people will be invited to your FR training session. The goal is to have a team of 6-8 persons well versed in Special Census procedures at the end of training. The actual numbers depend on the amount of work in your assigned area.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This chapter presents the tasks you must perform to prepare for and conduct FR training. Topics covered include:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Activities needing done a few days prior to the start of training, such as confirming the training site and reminding trainees of the date, time, and location of training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Verifying you have the materials needed to successfully conduct the training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Preparing to conduct training by learning how to use the SC-1204, Special Census Guide for Training Field Representatives.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Your responsibilities while conducting training, including how to set up the classroom for training and tips for staying on schedule.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Activities needing done at the end of training, including providing assignments, scheduling initial observations, and scheduling regular meetings.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Conducting an initial observation of each of your team members as they work their first assignment.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Activities Prior to Conducting Training' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=29, title='Training Your Team', content_len=1476
NEW_TITLE: 'Activities Prior to Conducting Training'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The governmental unit requesting the special census will locate and secure a site for your Field Representative (FR) training session. Closer to the start of training, the training site needs to be visited to confirm its availability on the dates needed, the hours the space is available, and its suitability.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'A few days before the start of training, each trainee needs to receive a reminder phone call regarding the date, time, and location for the training session.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Your manager may request your assistance in confirming the training site and/or placing reminder phone calls to the trainees.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'In addition, prior to conducting training, be sure to travel to your assigned Field Supervisor Area (FSA) and familiarize yourself with the area. All assignments for your team are located within your FSA.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This topic provides more information on:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Confirming the training site.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Placing reminder phone calls to trainees.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Becoming familiar with your FSA.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Confirming the Training Site' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=30, title='Activities Prior to Conducting Training', content_len=963
NEW_TITLE: 'Confirming the Training Site'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Your manager may ask you to visit the training site, as the date for training approaches. At the training site:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Confirm the site's availability on the dates needed.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Confirm the hours the site is available.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Ask if there are any requirements for entering the building/site.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Confirm the site's suitability by ensuring:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   The site is quiet, well-ventilated, and well-lit.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   There are enough tables and chairs for up to eight trainees.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   There is enough table space for each trainee's training materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   There are restrooms nearby.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   There is enough parking or public transportation nearby.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   The site is handicap accessible.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'After visiting the training site, if you have any concerns with the site's availability or suitability, notify your manager right away.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Reminder Phone Calls' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=31, title='Confirming the Training Site', content_len=822
NEW_TITLE: 'Reminder Phone Calls'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Your manager may request your assistance in placing phone calls to the trainees before the training session to:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Remind them of the date, time, and location of training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Confirm their attendance.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Your manager will provide you with a training roster, listing the name and phone number of each person scheduled to attend your FR training session.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Using the information on the training roster, call each person two or three days before the training session. Follow these guidelines when making contact:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Directly speak with each person. Do not leave a message with information about the training because they may never receive the message. You may leave a message for the person to return your call.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Introduce yourself and explain you are calling regarding the upcoming Special Census Field Representative training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Give the date, time, and location of training and confirm their attendance.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If they confirm their attendance, remind them to bring the appropriate identification document(s) to complete the Form I-9, Employment Eligibility Verification, along with a **legible photocopy** of the document(s).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Refer to the I-9 form for the types of identification documents each person needs to bring. Trainees need to bring one document from List A **[or]{.underline}** one document from List B and one document from List C.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If someone is no longer interested in the job, on the training roster, print *Will not attend* in the blank space next to their name and notify your manager immediately the person is not going to attend.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Whether the person confirms their attendance or states they are no longer interested in the job, enter the date you made contact on the training roster, in the blank space next to their name.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Becoming Familiar with Your FSA' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=32, title='Reminder Phone Calls', content_len=1757
NEW_TITLE: 'Becoming Familiar with Your FSA'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Your manager provided you a Field Supervisor Area (FSA) by Assignment Area (AA) map for your assigned FSA. This map displays major roads, names and boundaries of incorporated places, and the boundaries of each AA your team will work.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Before conducting training, use your FSA by AA map to travel to the FSA and become familiar with the area. As you travel through the FSA, mark the map in any way that will help you or your team members conduct work. Note items that might be a potential challenge, such as:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Groups of apartments.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Gated communities.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Housing/apartments with restricted access.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Rundown or dangerous neighborhoods.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   New construction.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Seasonal housing.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Access problems due to road conditions.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Living quarters behind the main living quarters.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Garages, sheds, and basements that have been converted to living quarters.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Dormitories and other group quarters, such as a prison or a nursing home.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Transitory locations, such as a hotels and motel, RV campgrounds and parks, marinas, racetracks, and carnivals.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Unconventional housing, such as tents or railroad cars.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Trailers on commercial or church property where someone may be living.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Anything else that might pose a challenge for team members during the Special Census.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Be sure to bring your FSA by AA map with you on the first day of training. At a break, or other appropriate time, have each trainee indicate the location of their home on the map. Mark the map to record these locations.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Having both potential challenges and each team member's home indicated on your FSA by AA map will aid you in making assignments, establishing a meeting schedule, setting up initial observations, and supervising your team.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Materials Needed for Training' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=33, title='Becoming Familiar with Your FSA', content_len=1740
NEW_TITLE: 'Materials Needed for Training'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Census Bureau has prepared several materials for conducting and participating in training to help ensure each Special Census training session is a success. This topic identifies the materials needed by you and the trainees during the training session.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
