LINE: '# Preparing to Conduct Training' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=51, title='Additional Materials Needed on the Last Day of Training', content_len=507
NEW_TITLE: 'Preparing to Conduct Training'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Preparation is the key to an effective training session. Preparing for training ahead of time will help you understand the subject matter and gain confidence in your ability to train. Showmanship and theatrics cannot mask a lack of knowledge of the subject matter. Your task is to make sure your team are grounded in Special Census procedures. Study the SC-1204, Special Census Guide for Training Field Representatives, and become familiar with all training concepts and materials. The more familiar you are with the subject matter, the more comfortable and confident you will become.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The guide for training tells you what to say and do. However, merely reading a guide does not make for an effective training session. The trainer must also keep the session upbeat.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This topic explains the organization of the guide for training and provides training techniques that will help you keep the attention of the class.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# The SC-1204, Special Census Guide for Training Field Representatives' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=52, title='Preparing to Conduct Training', content_len=915
NEW_TITLE: 'The SC-1204, Special Census Guide for Training Field Representatives'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The SC-1204, Special Census Guide for Training Field Representatives, is your guide for conducting training. It contains a training schedule, and the classroom lessons you will deliver to your trainees, and well as:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Instructions for conducting training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Tasks needing performed before and after each training day.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The guide for training is in your Kit SF-50.1A(FR), Special Census FR Instructor Kit. It is a verbatim training guide, intended to be read exactly as written, word-for-word to the trainees. We use verbatim training guides because they ensure uniform training for all training sessions conducted for the Special Census. Because all trainees receive the same training content, we can be assured that they are all following the same procedures. We also use verbatim training guides to help control costs and time.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The guide for training consists of a training schedule, a table of contents, and various training lessons.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Reviewing the Guide for Training' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=53, title='The SC-1204, Special Census Guide for Training Field Representatives', content_len=943
NEW_TITLE: 'Reviewing the Guide for Training'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When you start reviewing the guide for training, do not be too concerned about your presentation. Instead, concentrate on understanding the material presented.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If you do not understand a particular section, reread the portion of the guide for training that covers it or search for additional information in the Special Census Field Representative Manual or other reference materials provided. If necessary, ask your manager.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Once you understand the material, start working on your presentation. Conduct a dry run, or rehearsal, of the training. A dry run is your practice session. Read the text aloud, so you can hear what you sound like. Practice your delivery, set your timing, and become more comfortable with the flow of the training. Try to anticipate questions trainees are likely to ask. Make sure you know the answers to these questions before training begins.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Training Techniques' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=54, title='Reviewing the Guide for Training', content_len=870
NEW_TITLE: 'Training Techniques'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Merely reading the guide for training does not make for an effective training session. The trainer must also keep the session upbeat. The following training techniques will help you keep the attention of the class:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Stand up. Your voice carries better when you stand up. You also have a better vantage point to make eye contact with your audience of trainees, making it easier to detect signs of frustration, confusion, or lack of understanding.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Make eye contact with the trainees. Look up from your reading whenever the guide says (Pause), and at the end of each paragraph. Making eye contact will help keep the trainees engaged. When you look up, be sure to keep your place in the training guide by using your finger or a pen at the point where you left off.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If a trainee looks confused or troubled, stop and find out what the problem is before continuing.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Avoid distracting habits like jingling coins in your pocket or twirling a pen.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Speak clearly and make sure everyone in the room can hear you without difficulty.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Vary the tone in your voice. If your tone of voice stays at one level, trainees have a hard time staying focused on what you are saying and may become easily distracted or bored.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Read at a normal rate of speed.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Your Training Assistant' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=55, title='Training Techniques', content_len=1264
NEW_TITLE: 'Your Training Assistant'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Someone from the Special Census Office (SCO) will be assigned to assist you during your FR training session. This helps your training session run more smoothly and efficiently. Assistants can help set up the classroom and organize materials, hand out and collect materials, and handle minor issues while you continue training. Remember, they are there to assist you and not to provide actual training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Your manager will provide the name and contact information for your training assistant. Be sure to contact this person a few days before the start of your training session.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# If the Trainer is [Not]{.underline} the Team's Field Supervisor' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=56, title='Your Training Assistant', content_len=575
NEW_TITLE: 'If the Trainer is [Not]{.underline} the Team's Field Supervisor'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Keep in mind that if the team's Field Supervisor (FS) is not the trainer, the trainer will need to adjust the wording to reflect that the trainer is not the trainees' supervisor. For example, changing the words from *me* to *your supervisor* in the text.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Conducting Training' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=57, title='If the Trainer is [Not]{.underline} the Team's Field Supervisor', content_len=254
NEW_TITLE: 'Conducting Training'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'One of the most important tasks of the Special Census program is to conduct training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This topic identifies:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   How to prepare the classroom for training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Tasks needing conducted every day of training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Tips for staying on schedule.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   How to handle poor performing trainees.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   How to handle classroom observers during your training session.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Preparing the Classroom for Training' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=58, title='Conducting Training', content_len=358
NEW_TITLE: 'Preparing the Classroom for Training'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Setting up the classroom for training is your responsibility. On the first day of training:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Arrive 30 to 45 minutes before the training session begins.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Arrange seats and tables so each trainee can see and hear you:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   [Do]{.underline} [not]{.underline} rearrange the room unless you have received permission from the site to do so.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If you have any observers, seat them at the back of the room.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Set a blank name card (from your Kit SC-50.1A(FR)) at each seat and have a black marker nearby.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Check that lighting and ventilation are adequate.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Locate coat racks and hangers, water fountains, rest rooms, and lunch facilities so you can tell trainees where they are.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Determine the location of any smoking areas. Smoking is not allowed in the classroom.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Daily Training Responsibilities' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=59, title='Preparing the Classroom for Training', content_len=832
NEW_TITLE: 'Daily Training Responsibilities'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Every day of training, be sure to perform the following tasks:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Arrive 30 to 45 minutes before the scheduled start of training to be sure the classroom is ready for that day and to be available for any questions trainees may have. [On the first day of training]{.underline}, perform the tasks indicated in the previous section.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Document whether each trainee listed on the training roster showed up for training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Telephone any trainees who fail to show up for training (if instructed to do so). Enter the reason for not showing up on the training roster.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Conduct the training using the SC-1204, Special Census Guide for Training Field Representatives. Remember to read the guide for training word-for-word and to perform all exercises and activities.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Follow the training schedule and the time allotted for each lesson as closely as possible.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Perform any end of day tasks listed in the guide for training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Review the training schedule in the guide for training each evening to identify the lessons to be conducted the next training day. For each of these lessons, review the Lesson Plan Overview:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Review the Materials Needed, to identify the items you need to bring to training to successfully conduct the lesson. Contact you manager immediately if you are missing any materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Review the Trainer Notes, to be aware of any actions you need to take before, during, or at the end of the lesson. Contact you manager immediately if you are missing needed information.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Staying on Schedule' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=60, title='Daily Training Responsibilities', content_len=1531
NEW_TITLE: 'Staying on Schedule'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'During training, you must strive to keep on schedule. The SC-1204, Special Census Guide for Training Field Representatives, contains a training schedule. In addition, the Lesson Overview at the start of every training lesson includes the estimated length of time to conduct that lesson.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Staying on schedule is essential. Remember, your job is to set the pace and complete training in the time allotted. Here are several tips to help you stay on schedule:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Stress the importance of starting on time in the morning, and after lunch and breaks. Resume the training, whether everyone has returned.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Limit discussions. While you should encourage the trainees to participate in the training, keep all discussions focused and to the point. If a discussion is taking too much time, end it and tell the trainees time constraints require you to move on.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If a trainee asks a question that will be covered later in training, tell them to hold the question until the subject is covered later. You might also put the question in a *parking lot* for later discussion.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If you do not know the answer to a question, write down the question and tell the class you will get back to them with an answer. Be sure to follow through.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If a trainee persists in their question, ask them to see you during lunch or a break.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Always be sure to complete the entire training. Read the content of the guide for training exactly as written. Do not omit anything and do not add anything unless instructed to do so by your manager.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**The Field Exercise**' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'On the third day of training, trainees will perform a Field Exercise. Trainees will be paired up and work a real, production AA assignment. Before this day, prepare for the Field Exercise as follows:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Pair trainees up and determine which trainee in each pair will receive an assignment for the Field Exercise. A group of three trainees is allowed if there is an odd number of trainees.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Determine which AAs to use for the Field Exercise (use AAs near the training site to reduce travel time).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Assign one AA/assignment package to each designated trainee.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Gather and bring to training the materials needed for the Field Exercise:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Assignment packages (Address Register + questionnaire envelope(s)).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Forms SC-CQ, Special Census Continuation Questionnaire (Quantity: 5 per trainee).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Unlabeled Forms SC-Q, Special Census Questionnaire (Quantity: 10 per trainee).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If any trainees speak Spanish:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Unlabeled Forms SC-Q(S), Special Census Questionnaire (Spanish) (Quantity: 5).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Forms SC-CQ(S), Special Census Continuation Questionnaire (Spanish) (Quantity: 5).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form SC-IS(S), Information Sheet (Spanish) (Quantity: 1 pad).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Also bring to class the forms necessary for making a reassignment in case a trainee who was designated to receive an assignment for the Field Exercise does not show up for class.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If any trainee does not show up for class this day, adjust your teams for the Field Exercise (a trainee cannot perform the exercise alone). Trainees need to be in pairs or groups of three, when necessary. If the trainee was assigned an AA, re-assign the AA from that trainee to another trainee, if needed.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Handling Poor Performing Trainees' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=61, title='Staying on Schedule', content_len=3277
NEW_TITLE: 'Handling Poor Performing Trainees'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If a trainee does either of the following, contact your manager and recommend they be released:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Fails to complete the training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Demonstrates during training, or the Field Exercise, that they cannot perform the duties of a Special Census FR.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If you are instructed by your manager to release a trainee, do the following:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Explain the situation on a Form SC-225, INFO-COMM.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Be sure a final Form BC-27, Time, Attendance, and Cost Report, and Form BC-27A, Field Employee\'s Reimbursement Expenses, is completed by the trainee. Enter *Last day of work* in Item 10, Remarks. Trainees who do not complete training will be paid only for the time they spent in training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Classroom Observers' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=62, title='Handling Poor Performing Trainees', content_len=680
NEW_TITLE: 'Classroom Observers'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Staff from the Regional Office (RO), Census Bureau headquarters, and/or special sworn individuals may observe classroom training. If your training session will be observed, your manager will tell you in advance and provide the observer's name, if available. If an observer arrives and you have not been notified by your manager, please call the Special Census Office (SCO) immediately to verify the observer has been cleared properly. **Do not allow anyone into the training session who has not been approved as an observer.**' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Although you should not anticipate any problems, if you believe an observer's conduct is inappropriate, contact your manager at the first available opportunity and ask for guidance.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Generally, observers attend classroom training:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   To assess the comprehensiveness of the training content.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   To determine how well the trainees understand the information and procedures presented.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Observers are [not]{.underline} there to critique your performance as a trainer.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Observers receive specific guidance outlining what they can and cannot do during their observation. In general, observers:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Must listen and observe. They should not interrupt the classroom training to ask a question, clarify a procedure, and so forth.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   May ask you relevant questions about census procedures or the training itself during a scheduled break in training. Be sure to answer observers' questions honestly and to the best of your ability. If you do not know the answer, admit it. Ask your manager for an answer to the observer's question.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Must act in a courteous and professional manner.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Post-Training Activities' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=63, title='Classroom Observers', content_len=1640
NEW_TITLE: 'Post-Training Activities'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'At the end of training, there are several tasks you must complete before allowing the new FRs to leave for the day. Provide each FR with:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   An initial supply of work materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   An AA assignment (assignment package).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Meeting with each Field Exercise pair to review their work completed during the Field Exercise and schedule their initial observations.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'During each initial observation, you will schedule regular meetings with the team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Each of these tasks is described in this topic. In addition, this topic also provides information on what to do if you do not have enough team members to complete the work in your area.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Providing Additional Work Materials' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=64, title='Post-Training Activities', content_len=642
NEW_TITLE: 'Providing Additional Work Materials'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Provide the following initial supply of materials to each FR:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Forms SC-CQ, Special Census Continuation Questionnaire (Quantity: 25).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Unlabeled Forms SC-Q, Special Census Questionnaire (Quantity:75).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If any trainees indicated, they speak fluent Spanish:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Unlabeled Forms SC-Q(S), Special Census Questionnaire (Spanish) (Quantity: 5).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Forms SC-CQ(S), Special Census Continuation Questionnaire (Spanish) (Quantity: 5).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Providing Assignments' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=65, title='Providing Additional Work Materials', content_len=435
NEW_TITLE: 'Providing Assignments'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Provide an assignment to each FR. Refer to Chapter 3 in this manual for information on making assignments.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Anyone who received an assignment for the Field Exercise but did not complete it, must complete that assignment (without their Field Exercise partner) before starting another assignment.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Instruct each team member not to begin work on their assignment until their scheduled initial observation. Information on initial observations is provided in the next section of this topic.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'At your discretion, team members who performed well during training may begin work before their scheduled initial observation. These are team members who performed well in the following areas:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Classroom participation' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   On-time to class' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Completing the classroom exercises accurately' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Your review of work completed during the Field Exercise' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Performance on the Final Review Exercise' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Review Work Completed During the Field Exercise' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=66, title='Providing Assignments', content_len=888
NEW_TITLE: 'Review Work Completed During the Field Exercise'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Meet with each Field Exercise pair of FRs, to review their work completed during the Field Exercise. Use the Form SC-1130.1, Field Supervisor Checklist for Reviewing Materials, to review any completed INFO-COMMs, completed questionnaires, and the entries made in the Address Register.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Refer to Chapter 4, Topic 2 in this manual for information on conducting this meeting and using the Form SC-1130.1, Field Supervisor Checklist for Reviewing Materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Scheduling Initial Observations' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=67, title='Review Work Completed During the Field Exercise', content_len=453
NEW_TITLE: 'Scheduling Initial Observations'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Because your team are new to the procedures for canvassing and collecting data, you are required to conduct an initial observation of each team member while they work their first assignment. These initial observations assure us that team members are performing correctly the tasks learned during training and that they are following proper procedures. It also gives you an opportunity as their supervisor to provide immediate constructive feedback and correct errors.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Schedule an initial observation with each team member before they leave the training site.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Initial observations must take place during the week following training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Schedule earlier observations with those team members who did not perform well during training, during the Field Exercise, and/or on the Final Review Exercise.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Plan 2 hours for each observation. Be sure to allow time for driving between scheduled observations.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Use your FSA by AA map when scheduling observations to be aware of the location of each team member's assignment and to identify a meeting location nearby.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Refer to Topic 7 of this chapter for information on conducting initial observations.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'After conducting the observation, while still meeting with the team member, you will determine a regular meeting schedule.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Scheduling Regular Meetings with Each Team Member' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=68, title='Scheduling Initial Observations', content_len=1279
NEW_TITLE: 'Scheduling Regular Meetings with Each Team Member'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'During the Special Census program, you are required to meet with each member of your team each day they work. Because you will have several team members to meet with on a given day, you need to establish a regular meeting schedule with each member of your team.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'After conducting a team member's initial observation, while still meeting with them, determine a regular meeting schedule. Ask the days of the week they plan on working during the Special Census program. Remember, they can work any day, Sunday through Saturday, and are expected to work 25-30 hours, but no more than 40 hours, a week.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Together, determine a meeting location and time for each day of the week they plan on working. Use your Field Supervisor Area (FSA) by Assignment Area (AA) map to aid in determining a meeting location convenient to your team, so each team member does not have to drive too many miles. Possible locations include public buildings (libraries), commercial locations (fast-food restaurants, shopping center food courts), and public parks. Meet only at public places where there is no charge to conduct meetings.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If your FSA is large, reduce travel time by selecting two or more meeting places that are convenient for team members working in widely separated areas. You can meet with some team members at one location for a set period and then travel to the other location to meet with the other members of your team.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Try to schedule meetings so team members are not stopping work to meet with you, then having to return to the work area. Stagger the starting times of each meeting so only one person is there at a time. Plan to spend about 20 to 30 minutes with each member of your team.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Try to meet at the same location and during the same time each day. This will make the meetings easier to remember. Be sure both you and each team member write down the meeting days, location, and time. FRs should write this information where indicated on the Contact Information page in the front of their Special Census Field Representative manual. You should enter this information on the Meeting Schedules page in the front of this manual.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Be sure each team member understands that you must meet each day they work, and they are to notify you as soon as possible if they need to make changes to the meeting schedule.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If a team member notifies you, they will not be working on a previously scheduled day, ask if they will be working a different day and schedule a meeting for that day.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If a team member notifies you, they will be working but cannot meet with you at the scheduled time or location, determine a new time and/or location to meet that day.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Additional Team Members Needed' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=69, title='Scheduling Regular Meetings with Each Team Member', content_len=2652
NEW_TITLE: 'Additional Team Members Needed'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If, at the end of your FR training session, you do not have enough team members to complete the work in your area, contact your manager. An additional training session may be scheduled. Your manager or the Special Census Office (SCO) will arrange to have you or someone they designate conduct the training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Conducting Initial Observations' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=70, title='Additional Team Members Needed', content_len=306
NEW_TITLE: 'Conducting Initial Observations'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'An observation is a means for you to make sure a team member understands and carries out work procedures correctly. It is also a way for you to provide on-the-job training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'An initial observation should be scheduled with each member of your team at the end of training. Initial observations must take place during the week following training. Refer to Topic 6 of this chapter for information on scheduling initial observations.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'For each observation, you will observe the team member as they canvass their assigned area and conduct interviews at each housing unit address. **Observe the team member** **while they work five housing unit addresses and conduct at least one interview [OR]{.underline} for up to two hours, whichever occurs first.**' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'During the observation, you will use the Form SC-1222, Special Census Observation Checklist, which is a two-sided form (see Figure 1 on page [37](#_Ref140829356) and Figure 2 on page [38](#_Ref140829419)).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '[]{#_Ref140829356 .anchor}Figure 1. Image showing the front of the SC-1222, Special Census Observation Checklist.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '![](/tmp/media/image1.JPG){width="6.095544619422572in" height="8.48031496062992in"}' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '[]{#_Ref140829419 .anchor}Figure 2. Image showing the back of the SC-1222, Special Census Observation Checklist.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '![](/tmp/media/image2.JPG){width="6.302529527559055in" height="8.527559055118111in"}' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You will use this form to evaluate the team member's performance in four key areas:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   General procedures' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Canvassing procedures' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Listing procedures' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Enumeration procedures' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'At the conclusion of the observation, you will recommend to your manager that the team member either continues work on their own or is observed a second time. You may also recommend discussing other actions with your manager, including termination. Remember, you can only recommend a termination. Your manager will make the final decision.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The remainder of this topic provides instructions for using the Form SC-1222, Special Census Observation Checklist, to conduct an observation. This form in available in your Kit SC-50.1E(FS), Special Census FS Trainee Kit.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Completing the Observation Form Heading Items' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=71, title='Conducting Initial Observations', content_len=2106
NEW_TITLE: 'Completing the Observation Form Heading Items'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When filling out a Form SC-1222, Special Census Observation Checklist, always use a black ink ballpoint pen. At the top of the form, complete Items 1 through 8 before beginning the observation.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Items 1, 2:** Enter the name and employee ID number of the team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Items 3, 4:** Enter your name as the Observer, and your employee ID number.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Items 5, 6:** Enter the date and time of the observation. Be sure to mark **am** or **pm**.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Items 7, 8:** Enter your SCID and FSA number.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Item 9:** Mark the box for **Production** and enter the number of the AA being observed in the space provided.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Observation Form, Instructions' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=72, title='Completing the Observation Form Heading Items', content_len=605
NEW_TITLE: 'Observation Form, Instructions'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Making contact at an address is **not** considered as conducting an interview.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Instructions box provides instructions for both Production observations and Reinterview observations. You will always follow the instructions provided for Production: Observe the employee working five (5) housing unit (HU) addresses and conducting at least one (1) interview in the field OR for up to two (2) hours, whichever occurs first.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Instructions box also instructs you to complete procedures 1 through 4 in Section I to record your findings.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Observation Form, Section I -- Procedures' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=73, title='Observation Form, Instructions', content_len=537
NEW_TITLE: 'Observation Form, Section I -- Procedures'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Section I asks *Did the employee perform the following procedures effectively?* These procedures are grouped into four areas, each listing the items you should look for during the observation:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   General procedures: Make sure the team member is prepared for the day and follows procedures protecting the confidentiality of census materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Canvassing procedures: Make sure the team member understands the correct way to canvass blocks and multi-unit structures.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Listing procedures: Make sure the team member understands how to assign Action Codes and the correct way to list different types of addresses.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Enumeration procedures: Make sure the team member understands how to contact a respondent, conduct the interview, and complete the questionnaire.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'To the right of the listed items are two columns, **Generally performed the procedure** and **Did NOT perform the procedure**. Mark the appropriate box for each item. Use the space under the boxes to enter any explanatory notes. For example, a team member initially might not have followed a procedure. Then, after you pointed out and reviewed the correct action, they executed the procedure correctly throughout the rest of the observation.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Section II - Recommendation' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=74, title='Observation Form, Section I -- Procedures', content_len=1211
NEW_TITLE: 'Section II - Recommendation'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Use Section II to record the outcome of your observation. The available options are:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Continue assigning work:** You are satisfied the team member is following procedures correctly and can work on their own.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Additional observation:** You feel the team member does not fully understand the tasks they are to perform, and an additional observation should be conducted. If this option is selected, instruct the team member not to perform any work until the additional observation is conducted.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '**Consult manager:** You would like to discuss the observation with your manager. When talking with your manager, provide details about the observation, so they can determine the next steps, which may include additional training or termination.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Section III - Additional Notes' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=75, title='Section II - Recommendation', content_len=741
NEW_TITLE: 'Section III - Additional Notes'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'No matter which recommendation you select, enter in Section III an explanation for your recommendation and any information that contributed to your decision. If you have any reservations about the team member's capability, document your conclusions, and discuss the observation with your manager. Remember, you can recommend termination, but your manager makes the final decision.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'After completing the Form SC-1222, Special Census Observation Checklist, return it to your manager at your next scheduled meeting.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Making Assignments' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=76, title='Section III - Additional Notes', content_len=512
NEW_TITLE: 'Making Assignments'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Introduction' -> H1=True
MERGED_HEADING: 'Introduction' added to content of 'Making Assignments'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Your team will work the Assignment Areas (AAs) located within your Field Supervisor Area (FSA). It is your responsibility to make assignments and provide assignment packages:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   During your Field Representative (FR) training session, to trainees for the Field Exercise.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Following training, to each team member, on a flow, throughout the Special Census program.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This topic provides a description of the materials needed to make an assignment. The remaining topics of this chapter provide instructions for:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Making assignments for the Field Exercise (Topic 2: on page [46](#making-assignments-for-the-field-exercise)).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Making assignments to team members during the program (0 on page [49](#_Ref140829677)).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Moving an assignment from one team member to another team member (Topic 4: on page [53](#moving-an-assignment-from-one-team-member-to-another)).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You are also responsible for reviewing each team member's work progress and completed work, and for returning completed assignment materials to your manager. Refer to Chapter 4: on page [61](#meeting-with-your-team) for instructions for performing these tasks.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Estimated Time to Complete an Assignment' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=77, title='Making Assignments', content_len=1150
NEW_TITLE: 'Estimated Time to Complete an Assignment'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'A typical AA contains approximately 75 addresses. Team members are expected to complete three to four questionnaires per hour and are expected to work up to 30 hours per week. Based on these numbers, it should take, on average, two to three days to complete an assignment.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Assignment Materials' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=78, title='Estimated Time to Complete an Assignment', content_len=272
NEW_TITLE: 'Assignment Materials'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Use the materials listed below to determine and record assignments made to your team members. In addition to these materials, you also need a black ink ballpoint pen, provided in your Special Census FS Trainee Kit, for entering information on each of the forms.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Assignment packages -- one for each AA in your FSA' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Your FSA by AA map' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form SC-336, Assignment Directory' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form SC-20, Field Supervisor Management Record' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form SC-336.1, Reassignment Worksheet' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form SC-1019, Employee Listing by FSA' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The remainder of this topic provides more information on each of these materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Assignment Packages' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=79, title='Assignment Materials', content_len=601
NEW_TITLE: 'Assignment Packages'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You will receive one assignment package for each AA in your FSA, consisting of:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   One or more Address Registers (dependent upon the number of housing units in the AA).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   One or more questionnaire envelopes.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The questionnaire envelope contains one labeled Form SC-Q, Special Census Questionnaire, for each housing unit (HU) address appearing on the Form SC-920, Address List Page, in the Address Register. These questionnaires are used by team members when conducting interviews at housing units in the AA.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Address Register is a legal size (8 ½ inch X 14 inch) pressboard binder that opens from right to left. The following table provides a brief description of each item in the Address Register.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------' -> H1=False
LINE: '  Form                                     Description' -> H1=False
LINE: '  ---------------------------------------- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------' -> H1=False
LINE: '  SC-101A.1, Special Notice Page           Serves as a reminder that all information in the Address Register is confidential, and all entries made need to be clear and legible' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '  SC-940, Address Register Cover Page      Used to track assignment information and indicate work progress' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '  SC-114, Block List                       Displays the Block Number of each block within the AA' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '  SC-920, Address List Page                Displays the addresses of all known living quarters (LQs) - housing units (HUs), group quarters (GQs), and transitory locations (TLs) - in the AA' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '  SC-921, Add Page                         Used by your team to list HUs, GQs, and TLs found during their work that are not listed on the Form SC-920, Address List Page' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '  SC-901, Notes Page                       Used by your team to enter any significant notes about an address' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '  SC-435, Dependent Quality Check Record   Used by a separate quality control staff while performing dependent quality checks on the completed assignment' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '  Map Envelope                             Contains an AA Locator map, an AA map, one Block map for each block in the AA, and a Map Legend' -> H1=False
LINE: '  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Before giving an assignment package to a team member, you will partially complete the Form SC-940, Address Register Cover Page, to record the assignment of the AA. See Figure 3. Example of Form SC-940, Address Register Cover Page. on page [57](#_Ref140830403).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Your Field Supervisor Area (FSA) by Assignment Area (AA) Map' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=80, title='Assignment Packages', content_len=2745
NEW_TITLE: 'Your Field Supervisor Area (FSA) by Assignment Area (AA) Map'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This map displays major roads, names and boundaries of incorporated places, and the boundaries of each AA in your FSA. On Day 1 of FR training, you annotated your FSA by AA map with the location of each trainee's home. Since team members should receive assignments near where they live, you will use the location of each team member's home when determining which AAs to assign to a team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Form SC-336, Assignment Directory' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=81, title='Your Field Supervisor Area (FSA) by Assignment Area (AA) Map', content_len=394
NEW_TITLE: 'Form SC-336, Assignment Directory'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This report provides a listing, in numerical order, of every AA in your FSA, the person to whom the AA is initially assigned, and the estimated number of housing units in the AA. At the start of the Special Census program, for tracking purposes, all AAs in your FSA are assigned to you.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You will use this report throughout the Special Census program to keep track of which AAs you have assigned to your team, and which AAs still need to be assigned.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=82, title='Form SC-336, Assignment Directory', content_len=450
NEW_TITLE: 'Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The AA number of each AA in your FSA will be entered, in numerical order, in Section 1, Assignment Information, of the form.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This form was designed for your use. Throughout the Special Census program, you will enter data on this form, creating a single source of information for each AA within your FSA.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You will use Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record, to record:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   The assignment of each AA.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Daily work progress in each AA.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   The date you accepted the completed assignment materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   The date you provided the completed assignment materials to your manager.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'See Figure 4. Example of Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record. on page [58](#_Ref140830639).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Form SC-336.1, Reassignment Worksheet' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=83, title='Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record', content_len=696
NEW_TITLE: 'Form SC-336.1, Reassignment Worksheet'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Throughout the Special Census program, the status of every AA -- who the AA is assigned to, when assigned, and when completed - is tracked. At the start of the program, all AAs in your FSA are assigned to you (indicated on the Form SC-336, Assignment Directory).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When you assign an AA to a team member, you must report the assignment to the Special Census Office (SCO), using the Form SC-336.1, Reassignment Worksheet. On this form you will indicate the person previously assigned the AA, the team member receiving the assignment, and the date the assignment was made. Provide completed Forms SC-336.1, Reassignment Worksheet, to your manager at your scheduled meetings, for returning to the SCO.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Blank Forms SC-336.1, Reassignment Worksheet, are in your Kit SC-50.1E(FS), Special Census FS Trainee Kit. See Figure 5. Example of Form 336.1, Reassignment Worksheet. on page [59](#_Ref140830354).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Form SC-1019, Employee Listing by FSA' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=84, title='Form SC-336.1, Reassignment Worksheet', content_len=896
NEW_TITLE: 'Form SC-1019, Employee Listing by FSA'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This report provides the name, employee ID, employee type, address, and phone number of every person on your team. The report also lists any languages, other than English, each team member speaks. Knowing the languages spoken by each team member is important when you have an AA in an area where most of the residents speak a language other than English, or when you need a team member to complete a questionnaire in a specific language.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'See Figure 6. Example of Form SC-1019, Employee Listing by FSA. on page [60](#_Ref140830952).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Making Assignments for the Field Exercise' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=85, title='Form SC-1019, Employee Listing by FSA', content_len=532
NEW_TITLE: 'Making Assignments for the Field Exercise'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'During your Field Representative (FR) training session, you are responsible for making assignments for the Field Exercise, which takes place on the last day of training. To conduct the Field Exercise, trainees go out in pairs and together work the assignment during the allocated time.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Because trainees perform the Field Exercise in pairs, you will only make an assignment to one person in the pair. If the assignment is not completed during the Field Exercise, it remains with the assigned person for completion after training ends.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This topic provides the steps for making assignments for the Field Exercise. These assignments should be made the day before the Field Exercise is conducted. Instructions for providing these assignments to the trainees are included in the Form SC-1204, Special Census Guide for Training Field Representatives.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Refer to Topic 3: on page [49](#making-assignments-during-the-special-census-program) for instructions for making and providing assignments after FR training has ended and throughout the Special Census program.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Step 1: Gather Materials Needed' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=86, title='Making Assignments for the Field Exercise', content_len=1057
NEW_TITLE: 'Step 1: Gather Materials Needed'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The materials listed below are needed when making assignments for the Field Exercise. Refer to Topic 1 of this chapter for a description of each item.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Your Field Supervisor Area (FSA) by Assignment Area (AA) map' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form SC-336, Assignment Directory' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Assignment packages' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form 336.1, Reassignment Worksheet' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form SC-1019, Employee Listing by FSA' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'In addition to the materials listed above, you also need:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   A list of paired-up trainees, with an indicator of which trainee in the pair is receiving an assignment. Try to give each assignment to a trainee living near the training site, to reduce driving time for their completing the assignment after training has ended. (Because trainees work the Field Exercise assignments in pairs, only half of the trainees will receive an assignment)' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   A black ink ballpoint pen' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Step 2: Determine AAs to Assign for the Field Exercise' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=87, title='Step 1: Gather Materials Needed', content_len=892
NEW_TITLE: 'Step 2: Determine AAs to Assign for the Field Exercise'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'For the Field Exercise, select AAs located near the training site to reduce driving time, thus allowing trainees more time to work the assignment. Because trainees will work the Field Exercise assignments in pairs, you need to select one AA for every two trainees. (If there are an odd number of trainees, three trainees may work an assignment together.)' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Use your FSA by AA map to determine suitable AAs near the training site. For each of these AAs:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   On the Form SC-336, Assignment Directory, locate the AA number in Column (3), AA' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   In Column (9), FS ![Checkmark with solid fill](/tmp/media/image4.png){width="0.1527777777777778in" height="0.1527777777777778in"}, for that row, enter a checkmark to indicate the AA is being assigned.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Repeat this step until the necessary number of AAs have been selected.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Step 3: Record Each Assignment on Form SC-940, Address Register Cover Page' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=88, title='Step 2: Determine AAs to Assign for the Field Exercise', content_len=819
NEW_TITLE: 'Step 3: Record Each Assignment on Form SC-940, Address Register Cover Page'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Remember, trainees will work the assignments in pairs, but each AA is assigned to only [one]{.underline} person in the pair. For each AA selected for the Field Exercise:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Locate the assignment package for the AA.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   On the Form SC-940, Address Register Cover Page (located inside the Address Register), in Section 1, Assignment Information:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Verify your information is entered correctly in Row (a)' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   In Row (b), enter the name, employee ID number, and phone number of the trainee receiving the assignment. Enter the date (month/day) the Field Exercise is taking place in the Assigned To field.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Repeat these steps for each AA being assigned for the Field Exercise' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'See Figure 3. Example of Form SC-940, Address Register Cover Page. on page [57](#_Ref140830403).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Step 4: Record Each Assignment on Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=89, title='Step 3: Record Each Assignment on Form SC-940, Address Register Cover Page', content_len=826
NEW_TITLE: 'Step 4: Record Each Assignment on Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'For each AA selected for the Field Exercise:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   On the Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record, in Section 1, Assignment Information:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Locate the AA number of the assignment.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Enter the date (month/day) the Field Exercise is taking place, for the Date Assigned' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Complete the remaining three fields by entering the name, employee ID number, and phone number of the trainee receiving the assignment.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Repeat this step for each AA being assigned for the Field Exercise' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
