COMMITTED: order=91, title='Step 5: Report the Assignment on Form SC-336.1, Reassignment Worksheet', content_len=1028
NEW_TITLE: 'Making Assignments During the Special Census Program'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You will see references to GQ and TL assignments in this topic.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Following Field Representative (FR) training, you are responsible for making and providing assignments to each member of your team, on a flow, throughout the Special Census program.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This topic provides the steps for making and providing assignments to your team after FR training has ended and throughout the Special Census program.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If you need to move an AA currently assigned to a team member, to a different team member, refer to Topic 4: on page [53](#moving-an-assignment-from-one-team-member-to-another).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If you need to make assignments for the Field Exercise, refer to Topic 2: on page [46](#making-assignments-for-the-field-exercise).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Making Assignments' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=92, title='Making Assignments During the Special Census Program', content_len=710
NEW_TITLE: 'Making Assignments'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Make and provide team members one assignment at a time. Generally, you should not give an additional assignment to a team member until they have completed the current assignment and you have received and reviewed their work. However, if a team member has shown they can properly perform the work, consider giving them an additional assignment if one of the following situations apply:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   The team member is likely to complete their current assignment before your next scheduled meeting.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   The team member has completed their current assignment except for a few callbacks or issues that cannot be completed immediately.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Step 1: Gather Materials Needed' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=93, title='Making Assignments', content_len=623
NEW_TITLE: 'Step 1: Gather Materials Needed'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The materials listed below are needed when making assignments. Be sure to have these materials with you when meeting with a team member, so an assignment can be made on-the-spot instead of the team member having to wait until your next meeting. Refer to Topic 1 of this chapter for a description of each item.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Your Field Supervisor Area (FSA) by Assignment Area (AA) map' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form SC-336, Assignment Directory' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Assignment packages' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form 336.1, Reassignment Worksheet' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Form SC-1019, Employee Listing by FSA' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Black ink ballpoint pen' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Step 2: Determine which AA to Assign to the Team Member' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=94, title='Step 1: Gather Materials Needed', content_len=605
NEW_TITLE: 'Step 2: Determine which AA to Assign to the Team Member'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Use your FSA by AA map, annotated with the location of each team member's home, and Form SC-336, Assignment Directory, when determining which AA to assign to a team member needing work. When making assignments, always try to give team members assignments near where they live. We do this because they are more familiar with the area near their homes, and the governmental unit will save money on team member mileage and travel time to and from the assignment area.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   For a team member needing work, find the location of their home on your FSA by AA map. Note the AA numbers near this location.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   On the Form SC-336, Assignment Directory, locate the first of these AA numbers in Column (3), AA' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Look at the entry in Column (9), FS, for that row:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   No entry indicates the AA is available for assigning to a team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   A checkmark indicates you have already assigned this AA to a team member. Look for the next AA number near the team member's home on the Form SC-336, Assignment Directory, to see if it is available for assigning.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Once you determine the AA you will assign to the team member, enter a checkmark in Column (9), FS, for that row, to indicate it is now being assigned.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Step 3: Record the Assignment on Form SC-940, Address Register Cover Page' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=95, title='Step 2: Determine which AA to Assign to the Team Member', content_len=1252
