LINE: '#  Meeting with Your Team' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=108, title='Review Remaining Work with the Team Member', content_len=2624
NEW_TITLE: 'Meeting with Your Team'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Introduction' -> H1=True
MERGED_HEADING: 'Introduction' added to content of 'Meeting with Your Team'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You must meet with each member of your team, each day they work, at a location within your Field Supervisor Area (FSA).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The purpose of these meetings is to:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Discuss any issues and make every effort to come up with a solution to any problems.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Make sure they are making satisfactory progress on their assignments.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Review their work for consistency, completeness, and legibility.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Collect completed assignment materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Collect, review, and certify their completed payroll record.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Provide feedback on their performance, answer questions, and distribute new assignments.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Each meeting should last about 20 to 30 minutes. This chapter guides you in conducting the meetings and provides instructions for finalizing and returning completed assignment materials to your manager.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Create a Meeting Schedule' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=109, title='Meeting with Your Team', content_len=818
NEW_TITLE: 'Create a Meeting Schedule'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Following your Field Representative (FR) training session, you scheduled, with each member of your team, a meeting location and time for each day of the week they plan on working. See Chapter 2, Topic 6 for more information on scheduling these meetings.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You must meet with each member of your team, each day they work. Team members are expected to notify you as soon as possible if they need to make changes to the meeting schedule.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If a team member notifies you, they will not be working on a previously scheduled day, ask if they will be working a different day, in its place, and schedule a meeting for that day.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If a team member notifies you, they will be working but cannot meet with you at the scheduled time or location, determine a new time and/or location to meet that day.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Prepare for the Meetings' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=110, title='Create a Meeting Schedule', content_len=793
NEW_TITLE: 'Prepare for the Meetings'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Refer to Chapter 7 of this manual for tips that will help you manage your time effectively, be a good leader, and communicate effectively.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'In preparation for each meeting:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Wherever you see the *Field Supervisor Checklist* reference in this document you need to review the checklist for the operation you are managing, and they can be found in your kit.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Review any notes or action items from your last meeting with the team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Prepare for any counseling and/or retraining needing to take place.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Have the following items with you:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Assignment packages and all materials necessary for making assignments (listed in Chapter 3, Topic 3)' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   A black ink ballpoint pen (for signing and updating forms)' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Your Form SC-1130.1 Field Supervisor Checklists for Reviewing Materials' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   The Form SC-1130.1 Field Supervisor Checklists for Reviewing Materials was created to help you accurately review and update materials while meeting with your team members. You received this form during your Field Supervisor (FS) training. Be sure to follow all instructions provided on the form.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Remember to always wear your Census Bureau ID badge when meeting with team members.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Team Member Preparation' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=111, title='Prepare for the Meetings', content_len=1180
NEW_TITLE: 'Team Member Preparation'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Team members are to bring the following materials with them to make the best use of your time together.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   The assignment package for their current assignment: Address Register (including all maps) and questionnaire envelope (containing labeled questionnaires not yet completed)' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   All completed Forms SC-Q, Special Census Questionnaire, and any completed Forms SC-CQ, Special Census Continuation Questionnaire' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Any completed Forms SC-225, INFO-COMM' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Their completed payroll record, for the time worked since your last meeting.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   A list of any questions they have about canvassing, making contact, interviewing, payroll, or any other issues that pertain to their work.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   A list of supplies needed.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If they do not have these materials, conduct the meeting as best you can and remind them to be sure to have these materials with them at future meetings.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Conducting the Meetings' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=112, title='Team Member Preparation', content_len=870
NEW_TITLE: 'Conducting the Meetings'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Meeting Agenda' -> H1=True
MERGED_HEADING: 'Meeting Agenda' added to content of 'Conducting the Meetings'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When meeting with a team member, you will perform the tasks listed below, following instructions provided on the Form SC-1130.1, Supervisor Checklist Field for Reviewing Materials. Each task is briefly described in the remainder of this topic.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Review any completed Forms SC-225, INFO-COMM' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=113, title='Conducting the Meetings', content_len=262
NEW_TITLE: 'Review any completed Forms SC-225, INFO-COMM'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Review any INFO-COMMs the team member prepared for assignments in progress. Discuss any unresolved issues with the team member and determine solutions.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Review the team member's daily work progress' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=114, title='Review any completed Forms SC-225, INFO-COMM', content_len=151
NEW_TITLE: 'Review the team member's daily work progress'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Review all completed Forms SC-Q, Special Census Questionnaire and accompanying Forms SC-CQ, Special Census Continuation Questionnaire.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Review the Address Register for their current assignment.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Update your Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record, and the Form SC-940, Address Register Cover Page to indicate daily work progress.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Review the team member's payroll record' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=115, title='Review the team member's daily work progress', content_len=350
NEW_TITLE: 'Review the team member's payroll record'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Review and certify the team member's completed Forms BC-27 Time, Attendance, and Cost Report and BC-27A Field Representative's Reimbursement Expenses, for the previous workday.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Update your Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record, to indicate daily payroll information.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Provide feedback, answer questions, and provide new assignments' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=116, title='Review the team member's payroll record', content_len=286
NEW_TITLE: 'Provide feedback, answer questions, and provide new assignments'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Use the results of your review to provide feedback on the team member's performance, including work quality, production rates, and mileage claims.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Discuss any performance issues brought to your attention by your manager.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Inform team members of any procedural or schedule changes.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Answer any work-related questions the team member has.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Provide the team member with another assignment, if appropriate.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Review Completed Forms SC-225, INFO-COMM' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=117, title='Provide feedback, answer questions, and provide new assignments', content_len=423
NEW_TITLE: 'Review Completed Forms SC-225, INFO-COMM'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Collect and review any Forms SC-225, INFO-COMM, the team member completed since your previous meeting. INFO-COMMs are completed for several reasons, but must be completed when a team member encounters any of the following situations:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Address is inaccessible due to a natural barrier or natural disaster.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   A dangerous or threatening situation was encountered at an address.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   A language barrier prevented the interview from being conducted.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Respondent refused to be interviewed.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   They entered a group quarters (GQ), transitory location (TL), or targeted non-sheltered outdoor location (TNSOL) on the Form SC-921, Add Page.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   A Domestic Violence Shelter (DVS) was encountered.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Use the Form SC-1130.1Field Supervisor Checklists for Reviewing Materials, to conduct your review of the form entries. Review the explanation provided on the INFO-COMM with the team member, to understand the issue. Discuss any unresolved issues and make every effort to come up with a solution. If you are not able to resolve the issue, call your manager, while still meeting with the team member, for guidance.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Whether or not you are able to resolve the issue, complete the INFO-COMM as described in the Form SC-1130.1 Field Supervisor Checklists for Reviewing Materials, and distribute copies of the form as indicated.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Review Daily Work Progress - Completed Questionnaires' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=118, title='Review Completed Forms SC-225, INFO-COMM', content_len=1321
NEW_TITLE: 'Review Daily Work Progress - Completed Questionnaires'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Review all completed questionnaires:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Forms SC-Q, Special Census Questionnaire, and any accompanying Forms SC-CQ, Special Census Continuation Questionnaire.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Forms SC-Q(S), Special Census Questionnaire (Spanish), and any accompanying Forms SC-CQ(S), Special Census Continuation Questionnaire (Spanish).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The purpose of the review is to verify the questionnaires were filled out correctly and completely. If you discover any errors, the team member must correct them as soon as possible, preferably while you are meeting. If an error cannot be fixed during the meeting, return the questionnaire and corresponding continuation questionnaire, if any, to the team member for correction. [Do not]{.underline} separate questionnaires from their corresponding continuation questionnaires.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Use Section 2, Part A on the Form SC-1130.1, Field Supervisor Checklist for Reviewing Materials, to conduct your review of the completed questionnaires, and Section 2, Part B to conduct your review of any completed continuation questionnaires. After completing your review, use Section 2, Part C on the form to determine whether to accept the questionnaire. For questionnaires you do [not]{.underline} accept, you may request the team member:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Try again to complete the interview, or' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Hold on to the questionnaire until the remainder of the assignment is completed (at which time you will move the assignment to another team member to attempt the interview). Refer to Chapter 3, Topic 4 for information on moving an assignment from one team member to another team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Next, indicate the team member's daily work progress on your Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record, and the Form SC-940, Address Register Cover Page, following instructions in Section 2, Part D on the Form SC-1130.1, Field Supervisor Checklist for Reviewing Materials. It is important that these forms are updated with the team members completed work every time you meet. This information is used to monitor the team member's daily progress as well as overall progress in your FSA.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Provide all accepted questionnaires, and any corresponding continuation questionnaires, to your manager, who will return them to the Special Census Office (SCO). If there are any outstanding callbacks, ask the team member if there are any issues with completing the interviews. Remind them that callbacks need completed as soon as possible.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Review Daily Work Progress - The Address Register' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=119, title='Review Daily Work Progress - Completed Questionnaires', content_len=2406
NEW_TITLE: 'Review Daily Work Progress - The Address Register'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Review all work done in the Address Register since your previous meeting. The purpose of this review is to check for consistency, completeness, and legibility. Any errors discovered may indicate the team member does not properly understand procedures. All errors must be corrected by the team member as soon as possible, preferably during your meeting.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Use Section 3, Part A of the Form SC-1130.1, Field Supervisor Checklist for Reviewing Materials, to conduct your review of the Form SC-920, Address List Page, and Form SC-921, Add Page, in the Address Register. After completing the review, if the team member has not completed working the assignment, return the Address Register to them.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If a team member tells you they have completed their assignment, review the Address Register for the last day worked following Section 3, Part A of the Form SC-1130.1, Field Supervisor Checklist for Reviewing Materials. Once the Address Register passes that review, follow the steps in Section 3, Part B of the form to conduct a final review and then indicate your acceptance of the completed Address Register.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If the Form SC-920, Address List Page, in the Address Register, indicates a block in the AA, or the entire AA, contains no living quarters, verify the team member did indeed visit and canvass the block or AA, before following the steps in Section 3, Part B of the Form SC-1130.1, Field Supervisor Checklist for Reviewing Materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Provide the accepted Address Register to your manager, who will return it to the SCO.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If the assignment needs moved to another team member for completion (for example, there are outstanding interviews needing conducted by another team member) refer to Chapter 3, Topic 4 of this manual for instructions.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Review the Completed Payroll Record' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=120, title='Review Daily Work Progress - The Address Register', content_len=1742
NEW_TITLE: 'Review the Completed Payroll Record'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Review and certify the team member's completed Forms BC-27, Time, Attendance, and Cost Report and BC-27A, Field Employee's Reimbursement Expenses, for the last day they worked. The purpose of the review is to verify the entries are legible, complete, and reasonable for the work performed. If the payroll record contains errors, return the form to the team member for immediate correction.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Use Section 4 of the Form SC-1130.1, Field Supervisor Checklist for Reviewing Materials, to conduct your review. with the team member present. If the team member has not completed a Form BC-27, Time, Attendance, and Cost Report, for the last day they worked, have them do it now.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If a team member entered an expense on the Form BC-27A, Field Employee's Reimbursement Expenses, verify that it is a valid, reimbursable expense. Refer to Chapter 4 of the 11-55 (RO) Administrative Handbook for Employees, for a list of reimbursable expenses.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Team members must provide a receipt for any entered expense that is \$75 or more. If they entered such an expense on their payroll record, ask for the receipt. The original receipt, or a photocopy of the receipt, are both acceptable. If they do not have a receipt, the expense must be removed from the payroll record.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Consult your manager immediately if you suspect a team member is entering false claims for hours worked, miles driven, or expenses on their payroll record.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'After completing the review, follow the remaining steps in Section 4 to certify the form and update your Form SC-20, Field Supervisor's Management Record, with the team member's daily hours and mileage information. Provide all certified payroll records to your manager, for return to the SCO. Refer to Chapter 4 of the 11-55 (RO) Administrative Handbook for Employees, for information on certifying the Form BC-27, Time, Attendance, and Cost Report.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Provide Feedback, Answer Questions, and Provide New Assignments' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=121, title='Review the Completed Payroll Record', content_len=1869
NEW_TITLE: 'Provide Feedback, Answer Questions, and Provide New Assignments'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Use Section 5 of the Form SC-1130.1, Field Supervisor Checklist for Reviewing Materials, to wrap up the meeting. It is important to provide feedback to each team member on their performance. Performance includes quality of work and productivity. Your feedback should be based on the team member's daily work progress and submitted payroll record, as well as information from your manager and management reports. Refer to Chapter 5 of this manual for information on identifying performance issues, strategies for increasing production, and how to discuss performance issues with team members.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Be sure to provide positive feedback as well. Give praise for work well done.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If applicable, during your meeting inform the team member of any changes in procedures and/or schedules for the Special Census program.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Ask if the team member has any questions on anything discussed during the meeting or other work-related questions. Answer questions to the best of your ability. Note any questions you cannot answer right away and be sure to get back to them with an answer as soon as possible.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Provide the team member with another assignment, if appropriate. Refer to Chapter 3 of this manual for procedures for making assignments and providing them to team members.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Post-Meeting Activities' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=122, title='Provide Feedback, Answer Questions, and Provide New Assignments', content_len=1259
NEW_TITLE: 'Post-Meeting Activities'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Be sure to write down any notes, concerns, or action items from the meeting, to review before your next meeting with that team member. Prepare all collected materials (accepted questionnaires, completed Address Registers, INFO-COMMs, and certified payroll records) for returning to your manager as instructed in Topic 3 of this chapter.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Suspected Data Falsification' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=123, title='Post-Meeting Activities', content_len=336
NEW_TITLE: 'Suspected Data Falsification'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If, during your review of the assignment materials or payroll records, you suspect the team member may have falsified data, contact your manager. Remember, it is your duty to report any suspected data falsification to your manager immediately.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Preparing Materials for Returning to Your Manager' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=124, title='Suspected Data Falsification', content_len=243
NEW_TITLE: 'Preparing Materials for Returning to Your Manager'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When meeting with your team members, you will collect the following materials:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Accepted Forms SC-Q, Special Census Questionnaire, and associated Forms SC-CQ, Special Census Continuation Questionnaire.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Completed and accepted Address Registers (including all maps) and empty questionnaire envelopes.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Any completed Forms SC-225, INFO-COMM (whether resolved or having to go to the Special Census Office (SCO) for resolution assistance).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Certified Forms BC-27, Time, Attendance, and Cost Report and BC-27A, Field Employee's Reimbursement Expenses, and any associated receipts.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You may also have other materials needing returned to the SCO, such as:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Completed Forms SC-336.1, Reassignment Worksheet.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Completed Forms SC-1222, Special Census Observation Checklist.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Forms completed for conduct and/or performance problems.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Your completed Forms BC-27, Time, Attendance, and Cost Report and BC-27A, Field Employee's Reimbursement Expenses.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This topic identifies how to prepare these materials for delivery to your manager. Materials are expected to be returned to your manager, on a flow basis, throughout the Special Census program. Your manager will then return the materials to the SCO for processing.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Prepare a Messenger Envelope' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=125, title='Preparing Materials for Returning to Your Manager', content_len=1235
NEW_TITLE: 'Prepare a Messenger Envelope'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'All materials being returned must be inserted into a messenger envelope, except for the following:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Address Registers.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Any Forms SC-225, INFO-COMM, for issues not yet resolved or needing discussed.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Your completed Forms BC-27, Time, Attendance, and Cost Report and BC-27A, Field Employee's Reimbursement Expenses.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Messenger envelopes are available in your Kit Special Census FS Trainee Kit.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Print your name and FSA number in the space provided on the messenger envelope.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   If you are reusing a messenger envelope, cross out any information or other names written on the envelope, then enter your name and FSA number in the next available space.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Place the following materials inside the messenger envelope:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Accepted Forms SC-Q, Special Census Questionnaire, and associated Forms SC-CQ, Special Census Continuation Questionnaire.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Forms SC-225, INFO-COMM, that have been resolved.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Any INFO-COMMs for issues not yet resolved should [not]{.underline} be placed in the messenger envelope but handed to and discussed with your manager.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Certified Forms BC-27, Time, Attendance, and Cost Report and BC-27A, Field Employee's Reimbursement Expenses, and any associated receipts.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Completed Forms SC-336.1, Reassignment Worksheet.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Any other forms you must return to your manager or the SCO, such as:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Forms completed for conduct and/or performance problems.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Completed Forms SC-1222, Special Census Observation Checklist.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'At your next meeting, give your manger the prepared messenger envelope. Refer to Chapter 6:Topic 3: on page [86](#meeting-with-your-manager) for information on meeting with your manager.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Managing People and Performance' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=126, title='Prepare a Messenger Envelope', content_len=1709
NEW_TITLE: 'Managing People and Performance'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Introduction' -> H1=True
MERGED_HEADING: 'Introduction' added to content of 'Managing People and Performance'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You are responsible for managing your team and their performance. You are expected to:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Immediately address performance and conduct issues through counseling and/or on-the-job training.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Document all counseling and retraining sessions.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Discuss all performance and conduct issues with your manager.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Take appropriate action to release team members whose performance or conduct does not improve.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'While performance and conduct issues may be related, they are different. To determine if the issue is a performance or conduct issue, ask yourself if the cause is something the team member can't do or won't do.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Can't means lack of understanding or ability. This is a performance issue.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Won't means deliberately failing to follow a workplace rule or standard. This is a conduct issue.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This chapter describes how to identify and handle performance and conduct issues, including steps to release a team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Performance Issues' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=127, title='Managing People and Performance', content_len=947
NEW_TITLE: 'Performance Issues'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Performance issues are defined as issues caused by something the team member [can't]{.underline} do, because of lack of understanding or ability.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If the issue is caused by something the team member [won't]{.underline} do, such as deliberately failing to follow a workplace rule or standard, refer to Topic 3: of page [72](#conduct-issues).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Indicators of Performance Issues -- During Training' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=128, title='Performance Issues', content_len=340
NEW_TITLE: 'Indicators of Performance Issues -- During Training'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Possible indicators of performance problems during training are:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Consistently providing incorrect answers.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Difficulty learning procedures.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Difficulty with practice exercises.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Overconfidence.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Indicators of Performance Issues -- On the Job' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=129, title='Indicators of Performance Issues -- During Training', content_len=210
NEW_TITLE: 'Indicators of Performance Issues -- On the Job'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Performance issues include poor quality work and low productivity. Possible indicators of performance problems on the job are:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Multiple requests for help.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Questionable results.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Questionable payroll entries: Consider whether the hours claimed seem reasonable for the number of addresses worked and questionnaires completed, and whether the miles claimed seem reasonable for the area worked. If the hours and/or miles do not seem reasonable, discuss the situation with the team member. Perhaps they:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Do not fully understand the job.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Have a difficult assignment to work and did not notify you.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If you suspect falsification on payroll records, discuss your concerns with your manager immediately**.** Do not certify any questionable payroll records. Falsification of census documents and payroll records is illegal and constitutes grounds for dismissal.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Are charging time or mileage for personal business.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Are otherwise falsifying the pay record.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Overly high productivity.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Low productivity: A team member's low production could have several causes:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Poorly organized materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Not fully understanding the job.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Spending too much time on the job engaging people in conversation or asking needless questions.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Making repeated trips from home to the assignment and back.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Charging time for personal business.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Working too few hours.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Working an assignment that is difficult to canvass without mentioning the difficulty to you.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# How to Handle Performance Issues' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=130, title='Indicators of Performance Issues -- On the Job', content_len=1567
NEW_TITLE: 'How to Handle Performance Issues'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When you detect a problem, you need to handle the situation effectively. Generally, you must inform the team member of their performance deficiency, provide retraining, and advise that an improvement is expected within 24 to 48 hours or termination will result.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Be sure to discuss performance issues promptly with team members, to avoid problems in meeting operational deadlines.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Refer to Topic 4: on page [74](#providing-counseling-and-on-the-job-training) for guidelines for:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Discussing performance and conduct issues with a team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Counseling a team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Providing on-the-job-training (OJT) to a team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Documenting your actions and discussions.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Conduct Issues' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=131, title='How to Handle Performance Issues', content_len=683
NEW_TITLE: 'Conduct Issues'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Conduct issues are defined as issues caused by something the team member [won't]{.underline} do, such as deliberately failing to follow a workplace rule or standard.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If the issue is caused by something the team member [can't]{.underline} do, because of lack of understanding or ability, refer to Topic 2: on page [71](#performance-issues).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Indicators of Conduct Issues' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=132, title='Conduct Issues', content_len=340
NEW_TITLE: 'Indicators of Conduct Issues'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Conduct issues are often harder to detect than performance issues. They are usually discovered by direct observation. Examples include:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Consistently arriving late for or missing scheduled meetings with you.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Refusing an assignment.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Insubordination/Refusal to obey an order.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   The burden is on the supervisor to phrase the order in such a way that there are no options. Make it very clear that the work must be completed by a certain time, for example, **You must complete this by the end of the day**.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Violation of an agency rule or regulation.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Unacceptable interaction with the public such as being overly aggressive, argumentative, or otherwise irritating to respondents or co-workers.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Falsification of data.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Compromise of confidentiality.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Report Suspected Falsification Immediately' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=133, title='Indicators of Conduct Issues', content_len=826
NEW_TITLE: 'Report Suspected Falsification Immediately'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If you suspect a team member of falsifying information or revealing confidential information to a non-Census Bureau person, contact your manager immediately. Only your manager can decide whether an investigation and suspension should occur. If an investigation is approved, you must remove all Special Census materials from the person during the investigation, including their Census Bureau-issued ID badge.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# How to Handle Conduct Issues' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=134, title='Report Suspected Falsification Immediately', content_len=407
NEW_TITLE: 'How to Handle Conduct Issues'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When you detect a problem, you need to handle the situation effectively. Generally, you will counsel team members about conduct problems. Refer to Topic 4: on page [74](#providing-counseling-and-on-the-job-training) for guidelines for:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Discussing conduct issues with a team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Documenting your conversation with the team member on the Form BC-282, Documentation of Conduct and/or Performance Problems.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Team members may be released without counseling if conduct is severe enough to warrant immediate release, such as for divulging confidential information or falsifying data.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# A Team Member Refuses an Assignment' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=135, title='How to Handle Conduct Issues', content_len=590
NEW_TITLE: 'A Team Member Refuses an Assignment'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If a team member refuses to accept an assignment, ask the reason why and then contact your manager for guidance.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Do not force the assignment on the team member or threaten them with termination.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Do not provide the team member another assignment package or give this assignment package to another team member until you have discussed the situation with your manager.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Providing Counseling and On-the-Job Training' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=136, title='A Team Member Refuses an Assignment', content_len=367
NEW_TITLE: 'Providing Counseling and On-the-Job Training'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You must let each member of your team know how they are performing, both when they are doing well and when they need improvement. Providing feedback is an ongoing part of supervising. The goal is to encourage your team to do quality work and to correct any practices that may adversely affect the program.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When performance or conduct needs improvement, you need to offer suggestions and advice. If you are convinced that a team member cannot do the job, you must make a recommendation to your manager to release that person promptly.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The remainder of this topic provides guidelines for:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Discussing performance and conduct issues.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Counseling a team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Providing on-the-job-training (OJT) to a team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Documenting your actions and discussions.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Discussing Performance and Conduct Issues' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=137, title='Providing Counseling and On-the-Job Training', content_len=773
NEW_TITLE: 'Discussing Performance and Conduct Issues'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Census Bureau uses two primary techniques for improving performance or conduct: oral counseling and on-the-job training (OJT). Counseling and/or OJT should be provided immediately after the performance or conduct problem is discovered.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When providing counseling and/or OJT, follow these guidelines:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Show respect.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Get the team member's perspective.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Be honest, specific, and matter of fact.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Document the discussion on the Form BC-282, Documentation of Conduct and/or Performance Problems' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Be sure to clearly:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   State the improvement period. Generally, give team members 24 - 48 hours to improve, due to the fast-paced nature of census work.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   State the assessment and monitoring method that will be used to determine whether improvement has been made.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   State the consequences of continued poor performance and/or misconduct, including possible termination.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '```{=html}' -> H1=False
LINE: '<!-- -->' -> H1=False
LINE: '```' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Make certain to alert your manager and Employee Relations Branch (ERB) specialist when you need to counsel or provide OJT to a team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Counseling a Team Member' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=138, title='Discussing Performance and Conduct Issues', content_len=1086
NEW_TITLE: 'Counseling a Team Member'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Generally, counseling is the technique used to improve a team member's conduct. When counseling a team member, you should clearly and directly:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Describe the problem.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Provide both yourself and the team member an opportunity to describe the problem. Your description of the unsatisfactory behaviors or actions should include the:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Situation in which the behavior occurred.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Behavior you heard or observed.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Impact the behavior had on you, others, and/or the Agency.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When you are describing the problem, concentrate on the team member's actions, not on personality or presumed motives. By focusing your discussion on the actions, the team member is less likely to feel judged or attacked.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Give the team member an opportunity to provide an explanation for the conduct issue. This will help you to script your description of acceptable conduct.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Describe the acceptable conduct and the changes that are necessary.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Be very specific about the desired future conduct so that the team member knows how to improve.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Ask open-ended questions to ascertain whether the team member understands what is expected.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'After the discussion, be sure to prepare a Form BC-282, Documentation of Conduct and/or Performance Problems. This form will need to be maintained in the employees Disciplinary and Adverse Action File (DAAF), maintained in the Regional Office.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Providing On-the-Job Training (OJT) to a Team Member' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=139, title='Counseling a Team Member', content_len=1375
NEW_TITLE: 'Providing On-the-Job Training (OJT) to a Team Member'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Generally, on-the-job training is the technique used to improve a team member's performance.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You may be able to review the situation or procedure that is causing the issue while meeting with the team member. However, most performance issues require on-the-job training. Use the method that best suits the situation.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'To conduct on-the-job training, meet with the team member at an agreed upon place for no more than [two hours]{.underline}. During this period:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Observe as the team member performs their work.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Encourage the team member to refer to their Special Census Field Representative Manual to find answers to questions.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Explain any procedure the team member does not seem to understand.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'There are four general guidelines for giving effective on-the-job training, which when followed, will maintain the team member's self-esteem while helping them become more productive. This is the Tell-Show-Do-Ask Method described in the following table.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------' -> H1=False
LINE: '  Step   Method' -> H1=False
LINE: '  ------ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------' -> H1=False
LINE: '  Tell   Tell the team member the specific method to use to perform the task. Explain the task thoroughly. Break the task down into key parts or steps. Most persons find that learning and putting together several smaller tasks is easier than trying to learn one large skill all at once.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '  Show   Show the team member exactly how the task or skill is to be done. Explain specifically what you are doing, how you are doing it, and why you are doing it. Involve the team member by asking questions and getting feedback.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '  Do     Give the team member the opportunity to perform the task. Observe and provide encouragement, constructive criticism, and additional pointers on how to do the task. Encourage them to refer to their Special Census manual to find answers to questions.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '  Ask    Ask open-ended questions to gauge the team member's understanding. Ask them to explain the process or skill to you. Ask them if they fully understand the acceptable performance.' -> H1=False
LINE: '  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'After the session, be sure to prepare a Form BC-282, Documentation of Conduct and/or Performance Problems. If the team member is still unable to grasp the basic procedures, speak to Employee Relations Branch (ERB) specialist and your manager about releasing them.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Document Your Actions and Discussions with Team Members' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=140, title='Providing On-the-Job Training (OJT) to a Team Member', content_len=3077
NEW_TITLE: 'Document Your Actions and Discussions with Team Members'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You must document every performance and conduct issue, and the action(s) you took, on a Form SC-282, Documentation of Conduct and/or Performance Problems.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Be sure to include a description of the issue, the date it occurred, and the team member's explanation of the circumstances. If you gave the team member a timeframe to take certain actions, record the timeframe, circumstances, and whether the team member performed within your deadline.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Also document any other information, including the team member's attitude or tone of voice, any training you provided, and/or any suggestions you made. You will need to refer to this record if the behavior persists and becomes a repeat problem.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'When documenting an issue or conversation, be thorough, factual, and non-judgmental. Your role is to take action to correct the problem and properly document your actions, not to render judgments or opinions.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Releasing Team Members' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=141, title='Document Your Actions and Discussions with Team Members', content_len=898
NEW_TITLE: 'Releasing Team Members'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Due to the time critical nature of the Special Census, team members who show performance or conduct issues must be dealt with quickly. Team members whose performance is less than satisfactory are generally given 48 hours to show improvement. If there is no improvement, discuss termination with your manager and Employee Relations Branch (ERB) specialist. For team members having conduct issues, if, after counseling, the misconduct reoccurs, discuss termination with your manager Employee Relations Branch (ERB) specialist.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Team members can also be released involuntarily for reasons other than performance or conduct issues, including expiration of appointment and lack of work.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'This topic provides the steps for releasing a team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Reasons for Releasing a Team Member' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=142, title='Releasing Team Members', content_len=741
NEW_TITLE: 'Reasons for Releasing a Team Member'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Releasing a team member is necessary when:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   They cannot do the work, particularly after retraining.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Job performance continues to be unsatisfactory after discussing the matter with them.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   They persist in unacceptable conduct.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   They falsify work.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   They resign.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Although they have completed work successfully, there is no remaining work to be done. This occurs as the Special Census is winding down.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Remember to discuss all performance and conduct issues with your manager and Employee Relations Branch (ERB) specialist. You may recommend releasing a team member, but your manager and Employee Relations Branch (ERB) specialist makes the final decision.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Releasing a Team Member for Lack of Work or Expiration of Appointment' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=143, title='Reasons for Releasing a Team Member', content_len=677
NEW_TITLE: 'Releasing a Team Member for Lack of Work or Expiration of Appointment'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Team members are given time-limited temporary appointments with a specific not-to-exceed date. At the end of the appointment, team members should be released from census duty.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'On this date, meet with the team member to collect their Special Census materials. At the meeting:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Thank them for their help in performing the tasks assigned.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Collect all government property following the guidance provided in the Collecting Materials section of this topic.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Releasing a Team Member for Performance or Conduct Issues' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=144, title='Releasing a Team Member for Lack of Work or Expiration of Appointment', content_len=460
NEW_TITLE: 'Releasing a Team Member for Performance or Conduct Issues'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Provided below are the steps for releasing a team member from census employment due to performance or conduct issues:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '1.  To recommend terminating a team member, complete a Form BC-282, Documentation of Conduct and/or Performance Problems. If the termination is the result of performance and/or conduct issues, include what suggestions for improvement were made and what the outcome was. Provide the completed form to your manager and Employee Relations Branch (ERB) specialist.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '2.  Your manager will let you know if/when the termination has been approved by Employee Relations Branch (ERB)' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '3.  Once the termination has been approved, meet with the team member to inform them of the termination and to collect their Special Census materials (following the guidance provided in *Collecting Materials* on page [81](#collecting-materials) of this topic). Be sure to reassign any remaining work to another member of your team.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Informing a Team Member of a Termination' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=145, title='Releasing a Team Member for Performance or Conduct Issues', content_len=925
NEW_TITLE: 'Informing a Team Member of a Termination'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Your job is to meet with the team member and deliver the decision. These discussions are never easy. Your goal should be to preserve the team member's dignity and your own, and to avoid creating bitterness or resentment.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Releasing a team member is a very important and sensitive part of your job. There are specific rules and protocols that must be followed.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Here are some practical considerations for planning, conducting, and following up on a termination meeting.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Who?' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=146, title='Informing a Team Member of a Termination', content_len=468
NEW_TITLE: 'Who?'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Although you may consider having a manager or administrative representative present during a meeting, it is typically not necessary unless you anticipate problems such as an emotional or violent reaction.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# What?' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=147, title='Who?', content_len=204
NEW_TITLE: 'What?'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Plan what to say and gather all necessary documentation before the meeting. The following script can be used as a guide:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You are released from employment because *(state the performance or conduct problem).* You were given oral counseling and an opportunity to improve on *(dates).* Your *(performance or conduct problem)* has not sufficiently improved. I must collect all your census materials immediately or your final paycheck may be withheld.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The key is to briefly summarize the main reasons for release, recap the issued warnings, and the opportunities that were extended to improve their performance.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Tell the person to expect a copy of the separation personnel action form (termination or resignation) in the mail within two weeks from the effective date of the separation. This document can be used as proof of employment when applying for unemployment benefits at their local state employment office.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Where?' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=148, title='What?', content_len=912
NEW_TITLE: 'Where?'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Schedule the meeting in a suitable setting that allows for relative privacy and freedom from interruption. Conduct the meeting face-to-face to facilitate the collection of materials.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# When?' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=149, title='Where?', content_len=182
NEW_TITLE: 'When?'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Plan to conduct the meeting as soon as all documentation has been completed and approved.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Why?' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=150, title='When?', content_len=89
NEW_TITLE: 'Why?'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Preparation is key when terminating someone from employment. Careful planning can limit misunderstandings, anger, and accusations. However, if you have concerns about the team member's reaction to being released, work with your manager to determine additional safety precautions.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Conclude the meeting with a handshake and a sincere wish they will do well in the future.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Collecting Materials' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=151, title='Why?', content_len=370
NEW_TITLE: 'Collecting Materials'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'You are responsible for managing your team's inventory of Census Bureau ID badges, Address Registers, questionnaires, and other materials they received for the Special Census program.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Plan to collect all government property at the termination meeting:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Their Census Bureau-issued ID badge.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Any assignment packages in their possession (Address Registers (including maps) and questionnaire envelopes (containing labeled Forms SC-Q, Special Census Questionnaire).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Unlabeled Forms SC-Q, Special Census Questionnaires, and Forms SC-CQ, Special Census Continuation Questionnaire.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Confidentiality Notices, Information Sheets, Notice of Visit forms, and Language Identification Cards.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Payroll records (review and certify their final payroll record before leaving).' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Any other Special Census materials/forms in their possession, including the U.S. Census Bureau carrying bag.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If you are unable to collect all these materials during the meeting, set up a time to do so later that same day or the next day.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Advise them that there may be a delay in receipt of their final paycheck if they fail to return any government-owned property.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'If they fail to return the materials, they may be held financially liable. The criminal code of the United States also provides penalties for theft, embezzlement, conversion of, or willful damage to government property. Title 18, U.S. Code 641, provides penalties of up to \$250,000 and/or ten years of imprisonment.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Census Bureau is committed to using any lawful and reasonable means necessary to recover property owned by the federal government and to ensuring the security of all Title 13 data in a team members possession. If all supplies and equipment are not returned within 72 hours of notification to return those items, their collection may be referred to the proper authorities.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Keys to Supervisory Success' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=152, title='Collecting Materials', content_len=1848
NEW_TITLE: 'Keys to Supervisory Success'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Managing Your Time' -> H1=True
MERGED_HEADING: 'Managing Your Time' added to content of 'Keys to Supervisory Success'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'A Special Census is conducted on a tight schedule. To meet the scheduled timelines, you must be sure that your team completes their work in a timely manner. You must also manage your own work schedule so you can satisfy all your work demands without getting into an overtime situation. This chapter provides tips for managing your time and being an effective supervisor.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Guidelines for Effective Time Management' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=153, title='Keys to Supervisory Success', content_len=393
NEW_TITLE: 'Guidelines for Effective Time Management'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The following are some proven time management tips that have been used successfully in past censuses and tests:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Review and set priorities for job activities you need to do daily. This is as simple as creating a To Do list which identifies must-do tasks on a piece of paper. After creating the list, number each task in priority order. As you complete each task, cross it off the list.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Do not make unnecessary trips. Try to accomplish several job tasks during a single trip.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Establish times when your team members can call you for assistance and inform them of these times.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Assign a specific time and place to meet with each member of your team, each day that they work. Make sure that you and each team member agree on the meeting times and locations and that both of you write it down.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Be on time for all meetings.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Stagger meetings with your team members so they do not have to wait long to see you. Having a team member waiting around not only wastes time, but it affects their work schedule.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Being an Effective Supervisor' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=154, title='Guidelines for Effective Time Management', content_len=1024
NEW_TITLE: 'Being an Effective Supervisor'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'A good supervisor, in addition to being able to manage time effectively, also is a good leader, communicates effectively, and promotes workforce harmony.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Leadership Guidelines' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=155, title='Being an Effective Supervisor', content_len=153
NEW_TITLE: 'Leadership Guidelines'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'Leading your team effectively is very important. Follow these guidelines to ensure your success:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   **Plan your workday**. Make a list of the activities you have scheduled for the day and plan your day accordingly. Remember that you need to meet with your team members each day that they work and with your manager daily.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   **Do not put off making decisions and acting**. Do the difficult tasks first, to prevent problems become major problems. Act promptly on any problems that arise, do not let problems accumulate. Ask your manager for guidance if you do not how to handle a particular problem.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Make sure your team members complete a payroll record at the end of each workday.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   **Motivate your team to do a good job**. Always praise a job well done by highlighting work done, for example, without errors. Motivate team members that might need encouragement to do a better job. Always use a positive tone to motivate team members and avoid unnecessary criticism of their work.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   **Lead by example**. Always deliver on your promises, for example, if you say you will provide an answer to a question, do so promptly. Always be on time for your team member meetings.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   **Give praise for a job well done without showing favoritism**. As you praise team members for a job well done, praise equally all team members that perform well.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   **Be accessible to your team**. As you have a list of contact information for your team members, make sure your team has your contact information. When a team member calls you, be accessible and responsive to them.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   **Know your team, how to reach them, and how many hours a day they are working**. Always have a list with you that includes the names, telephone numbers, and addresses of each member of your team. You may sometimes need to communicate with them quickly if a new situation arises, such as a new procedure.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   **Treat your team with respect**. Treat your team the same way you would like to be treated. Do not allow any name calling or other situations that can be considered disrespectful.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   **Be ready to lend assistance**. Support your team as necessary by helping when needed. Follow up with team members in your meetings with any concerns they might have and address them.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   **Be honest and objective**. If you do not know an answer to a question, be honest about it but get the team member an answer. If you need to counsel a team member about some performance or conduct problem, do so objectively by only stating the facts of the problem.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   **Meet with each team member each day that they work**. Meet your team members in the field to review their progress, discuss issues, review their payroll record, etc.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   **Be alert**. Anticipate potential problems with team members that miss or arrive late for meetings, are performing poorly, or have a low production rate. Deal with these situations immediately.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Communication Hints' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=156, title='Leadership Guidelines', content_len=2901
NEW_TITLE: 'Communication Hints'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   The following tips will help you communicate more effectively with your team.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Listen carefully to what your team has to say about their progress and problems.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Ask probing questions to obtain accurate information.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Give specific instructions. Seek feedback to make sure they understand what you are requesting.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Point out mistakes privately and in a constructive and diplomatic manner. If possible, sandwich constructive criticism between positive comments.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Offer suggestions for avoiding the same mistakes in the future.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Praise team members for a job well done, preferably publicly.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Be honest and objective.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   When necessary, release team members in a professional and tactful manner.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Manage Your Workforce' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=157, title='Communication Hints', content_len=724
NEW_TITLE: 'Manage Your Workforce'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The census workforce reflects the diversity of our multi-cultural population. In managing your team, remember to:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Value differences' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Accept change.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Respect others' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Understand cultural differences.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Adapt communications as needed (different cultures communicate differently)' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Always consider how your audience might interpret your message.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Census Bureau has a long-standing commitment to the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO), the fair and equal treatment of all employees and job applicants. EEO describes the right of all persons to apply for, and be evaluated for job opportunities based on merit, without regard to race, gender, national origin, color, religion, sexual orientation, age, or disability.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'The Census Bureau will not tolerate any form of discrimination, including sexual harassment. All applicants and employees have a right to freedom from retaliation for filing an EEO complaint, participating in the EEO complaint process, or opposing unlawful discrimination. The EEO complaint process is a legal process designed to safeguard these rights.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# Meeting with Your Manager' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=158, title='Manage Your Workforce', content_len=1106
NEW_TITLE: 'Meeting with Your Manager'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: 'After your FR training ends and your team begins their work, you will meet with your manager every day. The purpose of these meetings is to:' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Discuss your teams progress and performance on the Special Census program.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Discuss any concerns or issues you have with a team member.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Obtain assistance with difficult or unusual situations encountered by your team while working.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Pass along completed materials, and certified payroll records, for returning to the Special Census Office (SCO)' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '-   Submit your completed payroll record for the previous workday.' -> H1=False
LINE: '' -> H1=False
LINE: '# The Meeting Schedule' -> H1=True
COMMITTED: order=159, title='Meeting with Your Manager', content_len=570
NEW_TITLE: 'The Meeting Schedule'
LINE: '' -> H1=False
